content.text:
I committed the change as 9879857a15 on `claude/printer-setup-ways-8564f7`; it is not pushed. JusPrin 1 is now an import source like OrcaSlicer, and the Printers step at first launch offers three ways to set up printers. Every check passed except one: I could not test choosing a folder by hand in the system folder picker in the real app.

**What changed**
- **Start-up copy removed:** JusPrin 1's setup is no longer copied at first launch. The welcome-back window and its JusPrin 1 sign-in check are deleted, and the sign-up offer no longer mentions the JusPrin 1 subscriber price.
- **JusPrin 1 import:** it uses the same importer, lists and result screen as the OrcaSlicer import. It brings printers, presets and printer connections, plus Bambu's network file when JusPrin 2 has none. It never brings app settings, and presets reload afterwards.
- **Which screen opens:** JusPrin 1's import screen if JusPrin 1 has printers, even when OrcaSlicer is found too. Otherwise OrcaSlicer's screen, otherwise the printer form. A file opened at launch still skips the step, and Back returns to the welcome.
- **"Other ways" links:** every printer screen has an "Other ways:" line, worded as on the boards. On the OrcaSlicer screen it replaces the "Choose my printer instead" button.
- **App not found:** a link to an app that wasn't found opens a folder picker, then that app's screen. A folder with none of that app's printers gets a message on the screen.
- **New menu item:** File › Import › "Import from JusPrin 1…" sits under the OrcaSlicer item and opens the same window as the OrcaSlicer import.
- **Where OrcaSlicer is looked for:** on Windows, also a `data_dir` folder in its install folder (its portable mode). On Linux, also the three Flatpak folders it has used. An upstream OrcaSlicer commit confirms `io.github.softfever.OrcaSlicer` was the old Flatpak id.
- **Merge check:** the merge check against upstream lists the same conflicting files before and after this change. In `MainFrame.cpp` a conflict already existed next to the menu items; my three added lines make it slightly larger, and keeping both sides resolves it with nothing lost. In `GUI_App.cpp` I only removed lines the fork had added, which puts upstream's text back.

**Tests**
- Home page: 158 tests pass. AI panel page: 696 tests pass. Both type-check.
- C++: 560 and 172 test cases pass, and the two shell-harness modes that cover first launch pass.
- The real app was run with a fake home folder, and I saved 11 screenshots:
  - both apps found, JusPrin 1 opens first;
  - each link between the three screens;
  - Back to the welcome;
  - the JusPrin 1 import result, then Home listing the imported printers;
  - the File › Import window;
  - only OrcaSlicer found;
  - neither found;
  - the folder picker opening for a missing JusPrin 1.
- The Bambu network file was copied, and the JusPrin 1 folder was left unchanged.
- The screenshots and a note on how to finish are in the shared notes folder, under `printer-setup-ways-screenshots/` and `printer-setup-ways.md`.

**Still open**
- **Folder picked by hand:** the background screen tools aren't allowed to act on the system picker, and two requests for full-screen control got no answer. So picking a folder, and the "found no printers in that folder" message, are only covered by Home page tests. The note has the commands to finish it.
- **Choices of my own to confirm:** a renamed copy from JusPrin 1 is called "(JusPrin 1 copy)". A folder picked by hand is forgotten after a relaunch.
- **Test harnesses:** they may now read the person's real JusPrin 1 folder (only read), because that folder has no variable. Their first-launch check picks "Choose my printer", so the result doesn't depend on that folder.
- **Untested:**
  - whether Bambu's network plug-in picks up the copied file without a restart;
  - the Windows and Linux folder lookups on those systems;
  - an OrcaSlicer zip unpacked outside its install folder, which only the folder picker can reach;
  - MSIX installs.

